# MAC for wlan0, set before wpa_supplicant starts. The AIC8800 has no MAC of its own and the driver
# randomizes the tail on every boot, so the router sees a new device (and hands out a new IP) each
# time. Pin one here. A good choice is the address stock Android used: it's on the vendor kernel
# command line as androidboot.mac=... (adb shell cat /proc/cmdline before you wipe Android), or
# pick any locally administered unicast address (second hex digit 2, 6, A or E).
# Empty = leave the driver's random MAC.
WLAN_MAC=""
